# Day 5 — Dry Lightning. 28 August. Dry thunderstorm 14:00–17:30. A lightning smoke on
# Harrow Ridge at about 16:30, bearing 104 from Kestrel. That night: the ear.

call D5_AM
  day 5
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Three days of nothing. Congratulations, you're a professional. Readings?
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
  > "Hang on." -> hang
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry bulb {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}.
DOT  Copy. That fuel stick's the driest it's been all summer.
goto plan
node hang
THEO Hang on. I'll get them.
DOT  Don't bother. I know what they say. They say dry.
node plan
DOT  Dry storms building this afternoon. Lots of lightning, not a drop of rain. That's the bad kind.
DOT  Eyes open from two o'clock. If you see smoke, sight it in the finder and call me. That's the job. That's the whole job. Basin out.
do errand Fire watch: dry lightning from 14:00. If you see smoke, sight it in the fire finder and call Basin.

call D5_STORM
  day 5
  time 14:10-15:30
  kind small
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. That's the first strike on my board. Count the seconds between flash and thunder.
THEO And then?
DOT  And then divide by five, and that's how many miles away it is, and then you feel very clever. Basin out.

call D5_REPORT
  day 5
  needs smoke_sighted, !smoke_reported
  kind initiated
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Smoke report.
DOT  Go ahead, Kestrel.
THEO Bearing {bearing}. About nine miles. Thin white smoke, single tree. Harrow Ridge.
DOT  Copy. Bearing {bearing}, about nine, single tree, Harrow Ridge.
DOT  ...Crew's rolling. Nice catch, Kestrel.
set smoke_reported
do errand_done
choice
  > "Is that it?" -> it
  > "My hands are shaking." -> hands
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node it
THEO Is that it?
DOT  That's it. Somebody else gets to run up a hill now. You get to sit. Basin out.
end
node hands
THEO My hands are shaking.
DOT  Everybody's hands shake, the first one. Augie's shook on his last one. Basin out.
end
node quiet
DOT  Basin out.

call D5_BINOC
  day 5
  needs smoke_seen, !smoke_sighted
  kind initiated
THEO Basin, Kestrel. I've got smoke. East-southeast, I think. A thin white column.
DOT  Give me a bearing, Kestrel.
THEO It's... east-ish.
DOT  The finder. The big round thing in the middle of your room. Point it, read me the number. Basin standing by.

call D5_PROSPECT
  day 5
  time 18:00-21:00
  needs !smoke_reported
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Prospect Lookout just called in a smoke on Harrow Ridge. You seeing it?
choice
  > "I missed it." -> missed
  > "I see it now." -> now
node missed
THEO I missed it. I was — I missed it.
DOT  That's what there are two of you for. Prospect's got it, crew's rolling. No harm done.
goto out
node now
THEO I see it now. Bearing about one-oh-four.
DOT  Copy. Prospect beat you to it, but the bearings cross nicely. That's how we find them.
node out
set smoke_missed
do errand_done
DOT  Basin out.

call D5_EVE
  day 5
  time 17:40-19:00
  retry 20:30
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Storm's moving off east. Evening readings when you can.
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_pm set gave_readings -> read
  > "Later." -> later
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}.
DOT  Copy. Air's tired. So am I. Basin out.
end
node later
THEO Later, Basin.
DOT  Copy. Basin out.

call D5_NIGHT
  day 5
  time 21:00-26:00
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Crew's got your smoke in a box. One tree. Out by morning.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Good.
branch told_ear_early -> early
DOT  Can I ask you something?
THEO Go ahead.
DOT  You say "say again" a lot, for a man who tunes pianos.
choice
  > Tell her. set told_ear -> tell
  > "Radios are bad." set deflected_ear -> radios
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node early
DOT  Your ear. The left one. Is it getting worse?
choice
  > "No. It's the same." set told_ear -> same
  > "I don't know. That's the problem." set told_ear -> tell
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node same
THEO No. It's the same. It's been the same since February.
DOT  February.
node tell
THEO ...My left ear went quiet in February. I woke up and it was just... gone. Mostly.
THEO They say it might come back. They say "give it time." I've tuned pianos by ear for nineteen years.
DOT  And you came up a mountain.
THEO I wanted somewhere nobody would ask me how it was.
DOT  ...And then I asked.
THEO And then you asked.
DOT  Okay. Thank you for telling me. I won't ask again. You'll tell me when you want to.
THEO I'll tell you.
DOT  Goodnight, Theo.
end
node radios
THEO Radios are bad.
DOT  Mm. Radios are bad. Goodnight, Kestrel.
end
node quiet
DOT  ...Okay. I'm here. That's all. Basin out.
